 kinda weird and very non-obvious. If it's intentional, please add a comment."],["dc963fa0_835c9bdb",48,-4,0,"Huh, this is kinda suspicious. Do you have any extra info about this? If this really can't be avoided, we should probably file a bug against the owners of this code."]],0,403],[7140380,20403,169,4.21,3.407,[[18,56]],[["ab020dfc_bed083be",46,0,0,"So this is the difference: We're now not checking `IsSyncFeatureActive` anymore. Most of what that does is redundant with other checks: E.g. we already CHECKed `IsInitialSyncFeatureSetupComplete` in…"]],0,404],[7141999,20403,43,1.341,1.058,[[18,57]],[["1cc0f6c2_bbd76a94",7,0,0,"That's pretty odd - any idea why we were only returning that for sync-the-feature before?"]],0,405],[7146299,20404,23,0.737,0.556,[[18,58]],[],0,406],[7146267,20404,155,4.21,3.407,[[18,59]],[["166059ad_738af8da",49,0,1,"I'm a bit surprised this was necessary - we shouldn't be running this test in transport mode on CrOS anyway, right?! Anyway, I think a better comment to add here is that signing out isn't supported…"]],0,407],[7150888,20405,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,60]],[],0,408],[7151123,20405,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,61]],[["a05c40d9_6ba3a1b5",50,0,0,"APPS and APP_SETTINGS are also effectively CrOS-only now, though I think we've never actually properly turned them off on WML - see crbug.com/40267153. So we could just scope the entire file to…"]],0,409],[7151099,20405,3,0.143,0.09,[[18,62]],[],0,410],[7151160,20405,10,0.421,0.3,[[18,63]],[["c83508c3_9ffe3a8b",51,0,1,"nit: This leaves one mental step to the reader (...and on ChromeOS, there's only Sync-the-feature)."]],0,411],[7150904,20405,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,64]],[],0,412],[7153640,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,65]],[],0,413],[7152765,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,66]],[],0,414],[7152764,20406,10,0.421,0.3,[[18,67]],[],0,415],[7152361,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,68]],[],0,416],[7153639,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,69]],[],0,417],[7152360,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,70]],[],0,418],[7151899,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,71]],[],0,419],[7152762,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,72]],[],0,420],[7152763,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,73]],[],0,421],[7152358,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,74]],[],0,422],[7152761,20406,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,75]],[],0,423],[7157643,20409,10,0.421,0.3,[[18,76]],[],0,424],[7156581,20410,40,1.341,1.058,[[18,77]],[],0,425],[7151999,20410,23,0.737,0.556,[[18,78]],[["a2af7359_e3c67627",7,-1,0,"I think we should create a bug (pretty sure a bug already exists for this) to fix this flakiness. Looks like it's stemming from autofill code. Skipping flakiness check is okay for this test since…"],["aeef0ee1_c0416739",52,-1,1,"nit, why not make the new element the last one in the tuple? That'd have avoided most of the changes in this file."]],0,426],[7166333,20410,16,0.737,0.556,[[18,79]],[["591f0046_2f263ab5",7,0,1,"Is that bug's title/description still accurate? Wouldn't SetupClientsAndSignIn() be the same as SetupSyncWithMode(SetupSyncMode::kSyncTransportOnly)?"],["cf263713_66a2e00f",7,0,1,"Could you add a bit more detail here? What's the goal of this CL specifically?"]],0,427],[7177303,20412,23,0.737,0.556,[[18,80]],[],0,428],[7204011,20420,5,0.259,0.185,[[18,81]],[],0,429],[7207187,20423,638,10.971,8.929,[[18,1.0,82,634]],[["0bb388f1_684c445c",53,-3,1,"Add the store param here too? (Or TODO for now)"],["262a6394_6da0545d",37,-3,1,"Since there's a few more instances of this below: Create a helper like `GetBookmarkSyncService()`?"],["41a4d7da_382cb2cf",37,-3,1,"Please specify the store here"],["4acbfaa0_51b1d53c",37,-3,0,"There's a bunch more fixture classes here that should also be addressed. Since this CL is large enough as it is, maybe keep them for a followup?"],["51eae9b8_5dd1d524",7,-3,1,"Was this to distinguish \"local\" as in \"local creation\" vs \"local store\"? FWIW, \"local creation\" is used fairly commonly (e.g. in `DataTypeEntityChange`), so if it's just that I'd stick with the old…"],["5db301c8_1aa8b1b8",37,-3,1,"Here maybe wait until the local creation makes it to the fakeserver? As it is, there's a race condition between the local creation and the remote creation. (Which probably doesn't really matter in…"],["67767ef7_a742c750",7,-3,0,"optional: Put this into a separate CL? There's some risk that the tests will be flaky on Android, and then the entire thing might get reverted."],["84d63c69_121258ff",37,-3,1,"Same here: Wait?"],["a0a52c5d_33c3d23f",37,-3,1,"`kSingleProfileIndex`?"],["e178d582_064eabb7",54,-3,1,"These should also be updated, but it can certainly be a separate CL. TODO for now?"],["fa124414_8167c9a9",37,-3,1,"Could you please undo the reordering? I do agree that the old order is weird and the new one is better, but doing this in the same CL as other changes makes reviewing very hard."]],0,430],[7205665,20423,98,2.361,1.866,[[18,83]],[["b2b9497a_3c8fae19",55,-3,0,"This makes sense, but I do wonder why it now became necessary. Can you explain?"]],0,431],[7224737,20426,29,0.737,0.556,[[18,84]],[],0,432],[7245859,20433,25,0.737,0.556,[[18,85]],[],0,433],[7210912,20433,45,1.341,1.058,[[18,86]],[["9e53c0f8_fbc21eb5",7,-10,1,"Any particular reason for removing this? I guess it's to make the parameterization simpler? It doesn't matter *much* but usually you'd leave the feature override in as long as the feature itself…"],["c215d31b_a285ea53",56,0,1,"nit: This name seems a bit weird; I can't quite parse it? Maybe just `UsePrimaryIcon()`?"]],0,434],[7252072,20433,37,1.341,1.058,[[18,87]],[],0,435],[7252710,20433,47,1.341,1.058,[[18,88]],[],0,436]]}